: false, "num_turns": 6, "subtype": "success", "api_error_status": null, "result": "I split `report.py` into a `salesreport` package. With `sample.csv`, the new output matches the original byte for byte.\n\n**Layout**\n- `salesreport/loader.py`: reads the CSV into a list of rows.\n- `salesreport/aggregate.py`: the sale amount calculation (quantity × price, then discount) now lives in one function, used by all three groupings. Grouping by region, product or month is a single function that takes the key to group on.\n- `salesreport/output.py`: builds the report text. The three per-group print loops are now one formatting function.\n- `report.py`: entry point only, 10 lines without blank lines and comments. The usage message and exit code 1 when no file is given are unchanged.\n\n**Checks**\n- `sample.csv` → `cmp` identical\n- no file argument → usage text same, exit 1 same\n- extra cases (no rows, all cancelled, no discount column, bad qty/price, short date, missing status) → all identical\n\nTwo of the original's quirks are kept on purpose, so behaviour stays the same:\n- A bad quantity or price still counts as 0.\n- A discount that isn't a number still raises an error.", "ttft_ms": 2390, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 42428, "uuid": "76cf060f-727b-4eec-9d84-f12e32511a46", "ttft_stream_ms": 1174, "time_to_request_ms": 414, "time_to_request_phases_ms": {"other": 10, "system_prompt": 13, "resume_other": 0, "process_user_input": 1, "input_attachments": 4, "input_hooks": 1, "transcript_persist": 16, "tool_pool_refresh": 1, "init_message": 3, "engine_pickup": 1, "message_prep": 0, "model_config_wait": 1, "autocompact": 1, "query_setup": 0, "model_gates": 349, "tool_schema_build": 7, "message_normalization": 0, "client_creation": 4, "request_build": 2}, "turn_start_resume_kind": "none", "process_turn_index": 0, "time_to_request_loop_lag_ms": 7, "time_to_request_cpu_ms": 280, "time_to_request_major_faults": 0, "input_attachments_detail": {"slowest_producer": "model", "slo